cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Vectorscope in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Vectorscope: a workbench for inspecting the vector medium of open-weight language models"
abstract: >-
  Vectorscope loads an open-weight language model locally and makes its internal
  geometry visible: embedding tables, projection head, attention patterns, hidden
  states across layers, and autoregressive generation. The Critique group
  implements contrastive activation extraction and forward-pass steering. Part of
  the Vector Lab family of research instruments.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Berry
    given-names: David M.
    affiliation: University of Sussex
repository-code: "https://github.com/vector-lab-tools/vectorscope"
url: "https://vector-lab-tools.github.io/vectorscope/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.7.3
date-released: 2026-10-27
keywords:
  - large language models
  - interpretability
  - vector space
  - critical theory
  - digital humanities
  - transformer
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - activation steering
